[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3969355162","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116815#issuecomment-3969355162","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116815","id":3969355162,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sl42a","user":{"login":"sockeye-d","id":106356149,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlbdtQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106356149?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d","html_url":"https://github.com/sockeye-d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T21:32:59Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T21:32:59Z","body":"I don't think it can be freed because the rid of the texture is never freed. What happens if you free rid? Does tex ever get destructed?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3969355162/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3969391133","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116815#issuecomment-3969391133","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116815","id":3969391133,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7smBod","user":{"login":"SNAKFRIEN","id":65283327,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MjgzMzI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65283327?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN","html_url":"https://github.com/SNAKFRIEN","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T21:40:45Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T21:40:45Z","body":"@sockeye-d I can manually free the RID of the texture, but from my understanding, Texture2DRD is supposed to do that automatically. Texture2DRD  should take ownership of the RID passed into set_texture_rd_rid, and its destructor then frees the RID when Texture2DRD goes out of scope.\nI would also assume that tex gets destroyed automatically after ```TestTextureFree()```, because it's a local variable in that function.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3969391133/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3969705601","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116815#issuecomment-3969705601","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116815","id":3969705601,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7snOaB","user":{"login":"NoctemCat","id":22471296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDcxMjk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22471296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat","html_url":"https://github.com/NoctemCat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T22:53:02Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T22:53:02Z","body":"Looks like it won't free underlying texture, it uses `texture_rd_create` inside `set_texture_rd_rid`. And it does free returned from it rid, but docs mentions that you will need to free the underlying texture yourself https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_renderingserver.html#class-renderingserver-method-texture-rd-create , the destructor also doesn't touch passed texture\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3969705601/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3969817826","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116815#issuecomment-3969817826","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116815","id":3969817826,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7snpzi","user":{"login":"SNAKFRIEN","id":65283327,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MjgzMzI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65283327?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN","html_url":"https://github.com/SNAKFRIEN","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T23:21:13Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T23:21:13Z","body":"@NoctemCat Thanks for looking into this. Looking at the source code, I think you may be right\n\n@AThousandShips Perhaps you want to weigh in. I noticed you liked sockeye-d's comment, but you also recently contributed to this pull requests which states that you should not manually free the RID after passing it to Texture2DRD: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116671","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3969817826/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3971795674","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116815#issuecomment-3971795674","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116815","id":3971795674,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7svMra","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T09:29:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T09:29:54Z","body":"I'll take a closer look today, might depend on how quickly the texture resource is freed, it *should* own it, but it might depend, it might also not be *that* texture that leaks, it might be some other texture in that chain ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3971795674/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3972322487","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116815#issuecomment-3972322487","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116815","id":3972322487,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sxNS3","user":{"login":"SNAKFRIEN","id":65283327,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MjgzMzI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65283327?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN","html_url":"https://github.com/SNAKFRIEN","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T11:13:51Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T11:13:51Z","body":"@AThousandShips I appreciate it!\n\nAs NoctemCat said, the current behavior does not free the RID you pass into set_texture_rd_rid. The code is a bit confusing to read, because Texture2DRD stores both a texture_rid as well as a texture_rd_rid (that threw me off anyway).\n\nSo either the current behavior is correct, and Texture2DRD _should not_ own the RID passed into set_texture_rd_rid, or the current behavior is incorrect, and it _should_ own the RID. Either way, the documentation should probably reflect that, once we figure this out.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3972322487/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3985509106","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116815#issuecomment-3985509106","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116815","id":3985509106,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7tjgry","user":{"login":"RemiPKFX","id":263344657,"node_id":"U_kgDOD7JSEQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/263344657?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RemiPKFX","html_url":"https://github.com/RemiPKFX","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RemiPKFX/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RemiPKFX/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RemiPKFX/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RemiPKFX/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RemiPKFX/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RemiPKFX/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RemiPKFX/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RemiPKFX/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RemiPKFX/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-02T16:41:46Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T16:41:46Z","body":"> this pull requests which states that you should not manually free the RID after passing it to Texture2DRD: [#116671](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116671)\n\nHey! Since I made the issue for the PR you mentionned, I thought I'd pop in and add some of the things I've observed.\n\nI'm using `Texture2DRD` as a makeshift buffer for reading in gdshaders, so my code needs to reallocate the rd_rid quite often when the buffer changes size.\n\nWhat lead me to believe that `set_texture_rd_rid` took ownership of the rd_rid it was given, is that if the current rd_rid is freed before creating a new one and setting it, an error is logged: \"Attempted to free invalid ID\". The implementation of that method is indeed quite confusing to read and debug, so at a glance it looked like something might be freeing my rd_rid.\n\nI've dug quite a bit into it today, and here's what I concluded:\n- Internally, `Texture2DRD` creates quite a few RIDs for textures, shared textures and texture views. These are all taken care of and freed internally, but one of them uses `RenderingDevice::_add_dependency` to link itself to the rd_rid given to `set_texture_rd_rid`\n- When I freed my rd_rid, its dependencies were freed as well (including that internal shared texture)\n- Later, when `set_texture_rd_rid` was called again with a new rd_rid, `Texture2DRD` tried to free its internal resources and threw the invalid ID error because the shared texture was already freed\n\nTL;DR: Currently `Texture2DRD` doesn't take ownership of the RID given in `set_texture_rd_rid`: it must be freed manually. ***However***, if the RID is still referenced in `Texture2DRD`, it must first be replaced by a new one, or by an invalid RID.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3985509106/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]